# Generated from the OSRS Wiki page "Transcript:Family Crest" by tools/quests/transcript_to_dialogue.py
0	section	Starting off
0	section	Dimintheis
1	line	Dimintheis	Hello. My name is Dimintheis, of the noble family Fitzharmon.
1	select	Select an option
1	option	Why would a nobleman live in a dump like this?
2	line	Player	Why would a nobleman live in a dump like this?
2	line	Dimintheis	The King has taken my estate from me until such time as I can show my family crest to him.
2	select	Select an option
2	option	Why would he do that?
3	line	Player	Why would he do that?
3	line	Dimintheis	Well, there is a long standing rule of chivalry amongst the Varrockian aristocracy, where each noble family is in possession of a unique crest, which signifies the honour and lineage of the family. More than this
3	line	Dimintheis	however, it also represents the lawful rights of each family to prove their ownership of their wealth and lands. If the family crest is lost, then the family's estate is handed over to the current monarch until the crest is
3	line	Dimintheis	restored.
3	line	Dimintheis	This dates back to the times when there was much in-fighting amongst the noble families and their clans, and was introduced as a way of reducing the bloodshed that was devestating the ranks of the ruling classes at that
3	line	Dimintheis	time. When you captured a rival family's clan, you also captured their lands and wealth.
3	action	Continues from "So where is this crest?"
2	option	So where is this crest?
3	line	Player	So where is this crest?
3	line	Dimintheis	Well, my three sons took it with them many years ago when they rode out to fight in the war against the undead necromancer and his army in the battle to save Varrock.
3	line	Dimintheis	For many years I had assumed them all dead, as I had heard no word from them, but recently I heard word that my son Caleb is alive and well, and trying to earn his fortune as a great chef in the lands beyond White
3	line	Dimintheis	Wolf Mountain, although I know not where.
3	cond	If the player lacks one or more requirements of the quest and has a combat level lower than 55:
4	box	Before starting this quest, be aware that one or more of your skill levels are lower than what is required to fully complete it. Your combat level is also lower than the recommended level of 55.
4	action	continues
3	select	Start the Family Crest quest?
3	option	Yes.
4	line	Player	Ok, I will help you.
4	line	Dimintheis	I thank you greatly adventurer! Also... if you find Caleb... please... let him know his father still loves him...
4	action	end
3	option	No.
4	line	Player	I'm not interested in that adventure right now.
4	line	Dimintheis	I realise it was a lot to ask of a stranger.
4	action	end
1	option	You're rich then? Can I have some money?
