0	section	Caleb
1	line	Caleb	Who are you? What are you after?
1	select	Select an option
1	option	Are you Caleb Fitzharmon?
2	line	Player	Are you Caleb Fitzharmon?
2	line	Caleb	Why... yes I am, but I don't believe I know you... how did you know my name?
2	line	Player	I have been sent by your father. He wishes the Fitzharmon Crest be restored.
2	line	Caleb	Ah... well... hmmm... yes... I do have a piece of it anyway...
2	select	Select an option
2	option	Uh... what happened to the rest of it?
3	line	Player	Uh... what happened to the rest of it?
3	line	Caleb	Well... my brothers and I had a slight disagreement about it... we all wanted to be heir to my fathers' lands, and we each ended up with a piece of the crest.
3	line	Caleb	None of us wanted to give up our rights to our brothers, so we didn't want to give up our pieces of the crest, but none of us wanted to face our father by
3	line	Caleb	returning to him with an incomplete crest... We each went our seperate ways many years past, none of us seeing our father or willing to give up our fragments.
3	action	end
2	option	So can I have your bit?
3	line	Player	So can I have your bit?
3	line	Caleb	Well, I am the oldest son, so by the rules of chivalry, I am most entitled to be rightful bearer of the crest.
3	line	Player	It's not really much use without the other fragments is it though?
3	line	Caleb	Well that is true... perhaps it is time to put my pride aside... I'll tell you what: I'm struggling to complete this fish salad of mine,
3	line	Caleb	so if you will assist me in my search for the ingredients, then I will let you take my piece as reward for your assistance.
3	line	Player	So what ingredients are you missing?
3	line	Caleb	I require the following cooked fish: Swordfish, Bass, Tuna, Salmon and Shrimp.
3	select	Select an option
3	option	Ok, I will get those.
4	line	Player	Ok, I will get those.
4	line	Caleb	You will? It would help me a lot!
4	action	end
3	option	Why don't you just give me the crest?
4	line	Player	Why don't you just give me the crest?
4	line	Caleb	It's a valuable family heirloom. I think the least you can do is prove you're worthy of it before I hand it over.
4	action	end
1	option	Nothing, I will be on my way.
1	option	I see you are a chef, will you cook me anything?
