0	section	Talking to Caleb after the quest
1	line	Caleb	I hear you brought the completed crest to my father. I must say, that was awfully impressive work.
1	line	Player	I believe your father mentioned you would be able to improve these gauntlets for me...
1	line	Caleb	Yes, that is correct. I can slightly alter these gauntlets to allow you some of my skill at preparing seafood by making them cooking gauntlets.
1	line	Caleb	When you wear them you will burn lobsters, sharks and swordfish a lot less. It will be a permanent modification however, so make sure this is what you want.
1	select	Select an option
1	option	Yes, please do that for me.
2	line	Player	Yes, please do that for me.
2	box	Caleb takes the gauntlets from you, pours some herbs and seasonings on them, bakes them on his range for a short time, then hands them back to you.
2	action	end
1	option	I'll see what your brothers have to offer first.
2	line	Player	I'll see what your brothers have to offer first.
2	line	Caleb	As you wish. Let me know if you change your mind.
2	action	end
0	section	Talking to Avan after the quest
1	line	Avan	I have received word from my father of your assistance to our family in this matter. You have my thanks for restoring our honour.
1	line	Player	Your father mentioned that you could improve these gauntlets in some way for me...
1	line	Avan	Indeed I can. In my long time searching for the 'perfect' gold I learned a lot about gold items. I can improve these gauntlets so that they provide more than normal
1	line	Avan	experience when smithing gold. I can easily modify these for you.
1	select	Select an option
1	option	That sounds good, improve them for me.
